# ESPHome for esp-component.yml's esphome job (esphome config, validating the
# ESPHome external component against esphome/tests/ac3forge-test.yaml).
# Regenerate the lock after any change here with:
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#     --output-file=requirements-esphome.txt requirements-esphome.in
esphome

# Not imported directly - esphome's dashboard pulls in starlette, which
# carries four disclosed CVEs at every version this graph can resolve (two
# high: an SSRF/NTLM-credential-theft path via StaticFiles on Windows, and a
# request.form() size-limit bypass enabling DoS). Confirmed NOT fixable by
# pinning forward: platformio (esphome's own embedded-build dependency) hard-
# caps starlette<0.53,>=0.19, and 0.52.1 - already the version an unpinned
# resolve picks - is the last 0.x release ever published; the next one is
# 1.0.0, which platformio's own pin refuses. Explicit here (not left to
# resolve implicitly) so this reads as a confirmed, accepted limitation
# rather than an oversight: this job only ever runs `esphome config` to
# validate YAML, never esphome's dashboard, so the actual vulnerable code
# paths (StaticFiles, request.form() against attacker input) are present in
# the environment but never exercised. Revisit once platformio raises its cap.
starlette==0.52.1
